---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Bio">
	<h1>Who am I?</h1>
	<p>
		My name is Nymph. I'm a Member of Technical Staff at Goodfire where I work on mech interp/inference systems and
		performance engineering. I work on speeding up research code and infrastructure, building systems to make it scale
		smoothly and efficiently, and distributed training/inference.
	</p>
	<br>
	<p>
		What I care the most about in AI is shifting the distribution of outcomes in a positive direction. To do that,
		we have to increase positive outcomes and decrease negative ones. To me these are most strongly represented in
		AI for science/medicine and AI safety, and I believe firmly that interpretability is an important tool in
		helping to push forward both of these incredibly important fields. It was actually Goodfire that helped me
		to see this! For now I think that safety/alignment is the more important application of interpretability
		and I'm thrilled that our current direction is more aimed at safety research. Doing this work here, now, is
		very fulfilling and engaging.
	</p>
	<br>
	<p>
    	Outside of work I like to spend time working on devtools (lol I know) and learning about whatever
        catches my interest. I have long standing interests in history, economics, science, and philosophy.
        It's important to learn about things outside of your expertise and try to place everything within
        a broader body of knowledge. Often the connections between things are more informative of how to think
        about solving problems than the thing divorced of its context. I hope that by spending my time learning
        and practicing seeing the connections, I can gain the ability to see them in unexpected places that lead
        to insights that I wouldn't have otherwise had.
	</p>
	<br>

	<p>
	    I also produce music using Ableton, make visuals with TouchDesigner, and program microcontrollers
		to drive LED strips based on music running off of my own custom PCB made in KiCad. I write my own raps
		and record them, I'm hoping to finally get a real project together at some point and play some shows.
	</p>
</BaseLayout>
